exit: 0
--- stdout
commandments freeze — Mark a file intentionally immutable, or lift the mark. A frozen file is still scanned (so cross-file rules stay correct) but never flagged and never rewritten.
Also answers to: unfreeze

Usage:
  commandments freeze <path>    stamp the file frozen
  commandments unfreeze <path>  lift the stamp — the file is a target again

  Idempotent: freezing a frozen file (or unfreezing an unfrozen one) reports and does nothing.

